  "qskyway.btn.traffic": "＋ Traffic",
  "qskyway.city.label": "CITY:",
  "qskyway.coverage.body": "— for the rest ({missing}) we have not yet located a published rule at all. That is a claim about our search, not about the airspace: rules are published as feeds, as map layers and as legal documents, and a missing feed is not a missing rule. Astana looked unregulated until we read the AIP instead of looking for an API.",
  "qskyway.coverage.full": "— every city here is governed by something its own regulator publishes: {ceilings} by an altitude-ceiling grid, {regimes} by a prohibition or permission regime. Where the rule exists only as a document rather than a feed, it was read from the document — \"no API\" is not the same as \"no rule\".",
  "qskyway.coverage.head": "regulatory layer: {withFeed} of {total} cities",
  "qskyway.err.cityLoad": "Could not load the city: {err}. Check that the backend is running (/api/qskyway/city).",
  "qskyway.height.suspect": "⚠ height in question:",
  "qskyway.hero.disclaimer": "An engine and a proof of concept, not certified aviation software. Flying in real airspace requires regulatory clearance (U-space / UTM / CAAC). Building data: OpenStreetMap (open, ODbL).",
  "qskyway.hero.eyebrow": "AEVION · the planet of urban skies",
  "qskyway.hero.lede1": "3D air corridors and auto-navigation for air taxis on top of a real digital twin of the city.",
  "qskyway.hero.lede2": "Buildings come from OpenStreetMap; restrictions come from the regulators' own publications where those exist.",
  "qskyway.impact.body": "Enforce that ceiling as a hard constraint and {strict} of {pairs} routes remain flyable. Both directions are counted separately — wind and corridors make A→B and B→A different flights. Pads standing where the regulator authorizes nothing automatically: {pads} — nothing can lift off there without ATC coordination. Measured across every route by the same engine that builds them, not typed in.",
  "qskyway.impact.head": "pad-to-pad routes fly a corridor that stays within the ceiling {authority} publishes.",
  "qskyway.just.above": "above the published ceiling",
