  "security.compare.audit.aevion": "Audit log on the device, signed line-by-line, exportable as JSON in one click.",
  "security.compare.audit.trad": "Audit log accessible only by support staff after a written request.",
  "security.compare.credit.aevion": "Credit limit gated by Trust Score — formula and inputs visible to you.",
  "security.compare.credit.trad": "Credit limit decided by an external bureau using opaque scoring.",
  "security.compare.device.aevion": "Account state lives on your device; the bank UI is a viewer.",
  "security.compare.device.trad": "Account state lives on the bank's servers; you query it through their UI.",
  "security.compare.headerAevion": "AEVION Bank",
  "security.compare.headerTrad": "Traditional bank",
  "security.compare.kicker": "Comparison",
  "security.compare.title": "Old bank vs. AEVION",
  "security.cta.body": "If you're going to put money in a wallet, you should know how it's protected. Open the bank, look at /bank/trust to see your reputation math, and read /bank/about for the broader story.",
  "security.cta.kicker": "Read more",
  "security.cta.title": "Security is part of the product, not a checkbox.",
  "security.faq.a1": "Your wallet state goes with the device, but you can always log back in from another device — the server holds your account anchor (Account-id + balance). The lost local data is the audit log + goals + signatures. That's why Layer 5 (export) exists: take a JSON snapshot every now and then.",
  "security.faq.a2": "The team can disable a specific account at the backend layer for fraud-response reasons (it's a regulated obligation). What we can't do is read your local audit log, see your goals, or alter past signatures — those are on your device only.",
  "security.faq.a3": "We're not under banking law in any jurisdiction yet — AEVION Bank is a creator-economy wallet, not a deposit-taking institution. AEC is an internal credit unit. Read the Terms before topping up at scale.",
  "security.faq.a4": "Not from our side — the keypair lives in your browser. Loss = loss. Backups are your responsibility (the export JSON includes the keypair material).",
  "security.faq.a5": "Email yahiin1978@gmail.com with reproducible steps and impact. We respond inside 72 hours and credit anyone who reports a verified issue in the changelog.",
  "security.faq.kicker": "FAQ",
  "security.faq.q1": "What happens if I lose my device?",
  "security.faq.q2": "Can AEVION freeze my account?",
  "security.faq.q3": "How is this different from a 'real' bank?",
  "security.faq.q4": "Is the QSign keypair recoverable?",
  "security.faq.q5": "Where do I report a security issue?",
  "security.faq.title": "Honest answers to security-paranoid questions",
  "security.headline": "Defence in depth, not paperwork.",
  "security.kicker": "Security model",
  "security.layer.anomaly.body": "The wallet flags four anomaly classes locally: unusually large transfer (vs. your rolling average), first-time recipient, burst of outgoing transfers, late-night transfer. Each gets a notification before the operation hits your statement.",
  "security.layer.anomaly.kicker": "Layer 4",
  "security.layer.anomaly.title": "Behavioural anomaly detection",
  "security.layer.biometric.body": "WebAuthn-backed biometric prompts gate transfers above a configurable threshold. The biometric never leaves the device — it's an unlock for the local QSign keypair. No fingerprint or face data is sent anywhere.",
  "security.layer.biometric.kicker": "Layer 3",
  "security.layer.biometric.title": "Biometric guards",
  "security.layer.device.body": "Wallet, audit log, signatures, goals, gifts, and recipient lists live in your browser's localStorage — never on a shared server. The bank renders from your device. Lose the device, lose the wallet (so back it up — see Layer 5).",
  "security.layer.device.kicker": "Layer 1",
  "security.layer.device.title": "On-device storage",
  "security.layer.export.body": "Help → Export wallet downloads a JSON snapshot of 17 localStorage keys. Re-import on any device to restore. No vendor lock-in: your data is yours to take.",
  "security.layer.export.kicker": "Layer 5",
  "security.layer.export.title": "Portable export",
  "security.layer.qsign.body": "Every transfer is signed via /api/qsign/sign immediately after success. Payload + signature are stored locally; you can re-verify any historical operation against /api/qsign/verify. Tampering shows up as a red 'mismatch' badge on the receipt.",
  "security.layer.qsign.kicker": "Layer 2",
  "security.layer.qsign.title": "QSign Ed25519 signatures",
  "security.layers.kicker": "Five layers",
  "security.layers.title": "How a transfer is actually protected",
  "security.lede": "AEVION Bank is built on five layers of guarantees — cryptographic, behavioural, and procedural. Each layer fails independently, so a compromise of one doesn't unlock the rest. No security committee, no vague 'we take it seriously' statements; just the actual mechanics.",
  "security.notDo.item1": "Store a server-side database of your transactions accessible by employees.",
  "security.notDo.item2": "Send your biometric data, fingerprints, or face vectors anywhere.",
  "security.notDo.item3": "Sell your spending data to advertisers or 'partner' merchants.",
  "security.notDo.item4": "Outsource credit decisions to a third-party bureau with opaque scoring.",
  "security.notDo.kicker": "Things we deliberately don't do",
  "security.notDo.title": "What's NOT in the trust model",
